/*
  core/masks/attentive_approve.spthy -- f_H for the Attentive mask, APPROVE_REQ action.

  An Attentive user VERIFIES an approval prompt before consenting: it only approves a
  prompt bound to its own session (kind = 'self'), and would reject an injected one.
  §6.2 derived-mask: RespMask(P,'Attentive') marks the response; the current-mask gates in
  core/transitions/mask_state.spthy forbid it while any degrade (Busy/Careless/Habituated) is
  active -- so a user already degraded on the KDF cannot verify here.
  !Approved(...,'Attentive') is the persistent history sigma8 reads (two of them => habituation).
*/

rule Approve_Attentive:
    [ !Prompt(P, pid, 'self') ]
  --[ Approve(P, pid, 'Attentive'), RespMask(P,'Attentive'), Verified(P, pid), Answered(pid) ]->
    [ !Approved(P, pid, 'Attentive') ]
